    <string name="gs_title">Google sign-in is not set up for this app yet</string>
    <string name="gs_body">Google needs to know this Android app before it lets it use Drive. This is a one-time step in your Google Cloud console:</string>
    <string name="gs_step1">1. Open console.cloud.google.com and choose the SAME project as the web app\'s OAuth client (Drive\'s hidden app folder is shared only inside one project).</string>
    <string name="gs_step2">2. APIs &amp; Services → Credentials → Create credentials → OAuth client ID → Application type: Android.</string>
    <string name="gs_step3">3. Enter the package name and SHA-1 below, then Create.</string>
    <string name="gs_step4">4. Check that the Google Drive API is enabled, and that your Google account is a test user on the OAuth consent screen if the app is in Testing.</string>
    <string name="gs_step5">5. Wait a few minutes, then tap Connect Google Drive again.</string>
